                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]An ARPG with no leveling up...[/h1]\nThat's certainly the first time I've ever seen that. This game's title should be changed to \"Loot, Die, Repeat\", because that's exactly what you do. In the first 3hrs of playing this game, I died about 15 times. And I can't progress past a certain point: a room with 3 enemy humans in it, since they are too quick and you run out of stamina/health before you can kill more than one... it's not a glitch or anything, it's just that the game is too difficult... attribute that to me being a bad player, or to the game's balancing not being up-to-snuff, but either way, I can't make it past that point and gave up after dying for the 10th+ time at that location (I LOVE ARPGs and consider myself a pro at them with probably 1000+ hours between Grim Dawn, Path of Exile and Titan Quest in total). And even-though I can't bring myself to recommending this game, because I didn't enjoy my time playing this game, I still think this game could be amazing if only it was turned into a proper ARPG (like the games I mentioned above). The game runs on the unreal engine so it looks pretty, but I just don't enjoy the game as it currently is... you simply die too easily and most of the progress you made on the entire level is reset when you die (you keep your items)... so if you reach a room which you simply find too difficult, then you are screwed... because unlike Diablo or any of the traditional ARPGs, you [b]don't gain levels in this game[/b]... so you can't just grind a few levels to become more powerful than your enemies... you HAVE to kill them with what you currently have and if you don't have the skill/luck/equipment to do it, then your game ends right there and you won't be able to progress any further... An interesting concept, but I MUCH prefer traditional ARPGs over this. The masochists out there who enjoy playing Dark Souls might enjoy this game too, but I'm not one of those people. And considering that the game hasn't received an update in 4years (since April2018), my guess is that the dev isn't inclined to make any changes/improvements to the game, so my above suggestions are pipedreams. https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZPp2AJmFWxI\n\nFor more reviews, visit my curator page: https://store.steampowered.com/curator/7851637/\nFor my full recommended list of games: https://steamcommunity.com/id/lfpg/recommended/",
